      "operands": [
        "strlen(cptr) + 1",
        "SNMP_MAXPATH"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "lt",
        "left": "strlen(cptr) + 1",
        "right": "SNMP_MAXPATH"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_includefile_operand_must_fit_snmp_maxpath",
      "fine_trace_step": 4,
      "description": "Root cause. In the `includefile` handler, the only operand validation is a blank-line check. When the staged operand is present but 4106 bytes long, vulnerable code still proceeds directly to path construction without rejecting names whose length already reaches `SNMP_MAXPATH - 1`."
    },
    {
